LGPL-3.0 BOUNDARY STATEMENT (ifcopenshell)
================================================================================

Working interpretation, recorded pending counsel review (see
research/COUNSEL_QUESTIONS.md); this section is a compliance posture,
not legal advice.

This product imports ifcopenshell from Python at runtime, which we treat as
analogous to dynamic linking. The LGPL-3.0-or-later obligations are honored
as follows:

(a) USER-REPLACEABLE DEPENDENCY. ifcopenshell is consumed exclusively as an
    ordinary pip/conda package dependency. It is never modified, vendored,
    statically bundled, or fused into a single-file frozen binary (e.g.
    PyInstaller one-file mode is prohibited for any distribution of this
    product). A user can replace the ifcopenshell package with their own
    build at any time.

(b) LICENSE TEXT AND ATTRIBUTION. This NOTICE identifies ifcopenshell and its
    license; any binary or on-premise distribution of this product must ship
    the LGPL-3.0 license text alongside it.

(c) NO REVERSE-ENGINEERING PROHIBITION. No license or contract term of this
    product forbids reverse engineering for the purpose of debugging
    modifications to ifcopenshell.

(d) ARCHITECTURAL DECOUPLING AT THE DATA/GRAPH EDGE (openBIM boundary).
    Proprietary rule-pack content is decoupled from ifcopenshell at a pure
    data boundary: rule packs are declarative artifacts (SHACL/Turtle shapes,
    and — per the openBIM boundary mapping in
    research/STRATEGIC_MOAT_ANALYSIS.md §1.5 — IDS documents referencing
    bSDD-published semantics at the interoperability edge). Rule packs
    contain no code, do not import or link against ifcopenshell, and consume
    only the extracted feature graph (RDF A-Box) that the extractor emits.
    This decoupling is designed to keep rule-pack content clearly outside
    the derivative-work boundary of the LGPL-licensed library under the
    working interpretation above; it complements — and does not substitute
    for — the LGPL compliance mechanics in (a)-(c), which attach to the
    runtime that DOES import ifcopenshell.

